  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890230",
      "title": "Managing State & TypeScript",
      "sourceHash": "d49fa95ddcaeeb817754002d63bfdf0c77de55ba2ba5e87bd1310a36c4255822",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.99,
          "en": "So it's time for useState because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.99,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "of course we need to manage this todos array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 9.75,
          "en": "with state so that when we change it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.75,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "this component re-renders and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 15.493,
          "en": "these todos items also re-renders and is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.52,
          "end": 19.14,
          "en": "And for this of course we do what we learned in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.14,
          "end": 22.763,
          "en": "We import useState from react like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.18,
          "end": 27.88,
          "en": "And then todos actually will be converted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.88,
          "end": 30.97,
          "en": "I will get rid of those dummy todos here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.97,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "And instead I will call useState here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.755,
          "end": 39.83,
          "en": "And, we now don't just get back todos here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.83,
          "end": 41.77,
          "en": "but we get back in array as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.77,
          "end": 45.91,
          "en": "which we can destructure where we get our todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.91,
          "end": 48.363,
          "en": "and this state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.33,
          "end": 51.22,
          "en": "And thanks to TypeScript we now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.22,
          "end": 55.33,
          "en": "for example see that setTodos if we hover over it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.33,
          "end": 58.7,
          "en": "is actually of type react dispatch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.7,
          "end": 61.48,
          "en": "which might not be 100% clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.48,
          "end": 64.39,
          "en": "but which is actually that state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.39,
          "end": 67.06,
          "en": "which we can call to change our state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.06,
          "end": 70.123,
          "en": "to dispatch a state update so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.4,
          "end": 77.32,
          "en": "Now useState of course can take an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.32,
          "end": 79.18,
          "en": "and that could be an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.18,
          "end": 80.8,
          "en": "And empty array initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.8,
          "end": 82.863,
          "en": "because initially we have no todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.53,
          "end": 88.51,
          "en": "But here we actually now introduced a subtle problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.51,
          "end": 89.94,
          "en": "if you write it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.94,
          "end": 92.443,
          "en": "And do you see which problem that is?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.93,
          "end": 97.15,
          "en": "The problem is that I'm just passing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.15,
          "end": 101.18,
          "en": "in an empty array as a default value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.18,
          "end": 105.35,
          "en": "But TypeScript is not able to infer which types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.35,
          "end": 109.12,
          "en": "of values should be accepted in that array eventually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.12,
          "end": 114.07300000000001,
          "en": "That's why todos at the moment is of type, never array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.33,
          "end": 118.78,
          "en": "Of which basically means it always must be an empty array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.78,
          "end": 121.41,
          "en": "No values are allowed in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.41,
          "end": 125.29,
          "en": "That's what this strange never type means here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.29,
          "end": 128.01,
          "en": "And that's of course not what we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.01,
          "end": 130.55,
          "en": "But TypeScript infers this type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.55,
          "end": 133.68,
          "en": "because it's not able to infer that this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 137.72,
          "en": "should be an array of todos for example, eventually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.72,
          "end": 140.943,
          "en": "Because the initial value has no information about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 145.31,
          "en": "To make it clear that we initially have an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.31,
          "end": 148.16,
          "en": "but that eventually we wanna have an array full",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.16,
          "end": 149.68,
          "en": "of to-do items here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.68,
          "end": 153.25,
          "en": "we again need to tell TypeScript somehow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.25,
          "end": 156.984,
          "en": "And we can tell TypeScript because useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.984,
          "end": 158.26,
          "en": "this useState function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.26,
          "end": 161.01,
          "en": "out of the box is a generic function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.01,
          "end": 163.57999999999998,
          "en": "It is generic for exactly this reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.57999999999998,
          "end": 165.88,
          "en": "so that we can set the type of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.88,
          "end": 168.393,
          "en": "we eventually wanna store in this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.27,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "So we add angle brackets again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 174.56,
          "en": "and now we wanna make it clear that the kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.56,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "of data managed by the state will be an array of todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 180.66,
          "en": "We do this by using our todo type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 183.853,
          "en": "from that models folder and then square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.9,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "That means that this state will manage an array of todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "Initially it's an empty array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 191.99,
          "en": "because that's all define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.056,
          "end": 195.13,
          "en": "that does not conflict with this type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.13,
          "end": 198.54,
          "en": "But if we do add items to this array eventually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.54,
          "end": 200.32999999999998,
          "en": "they have to be todo items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.32999999999998,
          "end": 203.36,
          "en": "Not strings, not numbers, todo items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.36,
          "end": 205.95,
          "en": "which have to shape off the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.95,
          "end": 208.703,
          "en": "todo object clause here, we created here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.69,
          "end": 213.373,
          "en": "And now that's the proper way of defining this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.25,
          "end": 216.25,
          "en": "Now in add todo handler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.25,
          "end": 220.37,
          "en": "we then wanna create our newTodo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.37,
          "end": 224.35,
          "en": "by calling newTodo and passing in the todo text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.09,
          "end": 229.49,
          "en": "as a value to the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.49,
          "end": 233.803,
          "en": "And then we wanna call a setTodos and update our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 238.31,
          "en": "Now here, I wanna use my old todos state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.31,
          "end": 241.85,
          "en": "so the existing array and add this new todo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.85,
          "end": 243.94,
          "en": "and you learned that if you wanna update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.94,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "your state based on the previous state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 251.22,
          "en": "you should use this function form of updating your state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.22,
          "end": 255.27,
          "en": "And in this function you get the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.27,
          "end": 257.27,
          "en": "so to say, or to previous state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.27,
          "end": 259.66,
          "en": "depending on how you wanna look at it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.66,
          "end": 262.87,
          "en": "and then you need to return your updated state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.87,
          "end": 263.703,
          "en": "So in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 263.703,
          "end": 265.58,
          "en": "I'll return previous todos, concat, newTodo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.58,
          "end": 269.01,
          "en": "Concat is a method which we can call,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.73,
          "end": 274.17,
          "en": "that will create a new array, which we should do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.17,
          "end": 276.25,
          "en": "We should not mutate the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.25,
          "end": 278.4,
          "en": "We should return a new array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.4,
          "end": 281.87,
          "en": "which then will be used as a new state by react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.87,
          "end": 284.35,
          "en": "and this new array, thanks to concat,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.35,
          "end": 285.86,
          "en": "contains this newTodo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.78,
          "end": 290.983,
          "en": "That's how we can properly update the state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.98,
          "end": 294.08,
          "en": "And with all that in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.08,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "if we now save this and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 299.48,
          "en": "I got this unstyled form here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.48,
          "end": 301.77,
          "en": "and no todo list at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.77,
          "end": 305.97,
          "en": "but if I then enter a Learn React here, then this is added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.97,
          "end": 309.49,
          "en": "And if I add Learn TypeScript, this also is added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.49,
          "end": 311.163,
          "en": "So that is working.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
